EXT. DESERT CANYON FLOOR - DAY

Orange rock, white sky. A dry wash cuts the canyon floor. A crashed single-engine plane lies nose-down in the sand, one wing bent.

Four survivors sit in the narrow shade of the other wing.

RIGOBERTO "RIGO" SALAZAR (40s, pilot, blood-crusted shirt) tears a seat cushion for padding. A WOMAN IN A BLUE BLAZER (30s, torn sleeve) rations water into a tin cap. A HEAVYSET MAN (50s, glasses cracked) stares at the horizon. A teenage GIRL (15, headphones around her neck) draws in the dust with a stick.

The woman hands the cap to the man. He sips and passes it to the girl. She drinks, hesitates, and offers it to Rigo, who shakes his head.

RIGO
Keep it.

WOMAN
You haven't had any.

RIGO
I'm fine.

WOMAN
You're bleeding.

RIGO
It's old blood.

She takes the cap back. He looks at the others and clears his throat.

RIGO (CONT'D)
We stay with the plane. They look for planes.

HEAVYSET MAN
Who's they?

RIGO
Search and rescue.

HEAVYSET MAN
They know we're down?

RIGO
They will.

The girl scratches a circle in the sand. The woman watches it. The man in glasses looks at the girl, and then at the sky, and then at his hands.

WOMAN
He's lying.

HEAVYSET MAN
Who?

WOMAN
The pilot.

RIGO
I'm Rigo.

WOMAN
You're lying, Rigo.

RIGO
I'm telling the truth as I know it.

The Heavyset Man lowers his head. A single dust devil rises from the wash, spins across the canyon floor, and dies against the wreck. Nobody moves.

GIRL
(very quiet)
My name's Tess.

Everyone looks at her.

TESS
In case it matters.

WOMAN
It matters, Tess.

TESS
It's just. Nobody asked.

The Heavyset Man lifts his head.

HEAVYSET MAN
I'm Gideon.

The Woman in the Blue Blazer closes her eyes.

WOMAN
(after a moment)
Imani.

The four of them sit in the narrow shade, strangers with names.

IMANI
Rigo. How far to the road?

RIGO
Far enough.
